From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:20:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 007/342] mmc: add Amlogic Meson GX SD/eMMC host controller
 driver

mmc_bus_interface for the "amlogic,meson-gx-mmc" SD_EMMC controller of the
S905 (ODROID-C2), attached through the device tree:

- polled completion, one descriptor per command written into the CMD_*
  registers (CMD_ARG starts it), DMA with explicit cache maintenance through
  the physical map, multi-block transfers ended with CMD12
- 400 kHz from the 24 MHz crystal for identification, 1 GHz/40 = 25 MHz
  after; core phase 180 degrees as needed on the ODROID-C2
- 136-bit responses shifted to drop the CRC byte, as the MMC stack expects
- register address translated through the parent buses' "ranges"
- skips device tree nodes with status "disabled" (sd_emmc_a's clock is
  gated; touching it stalls the bus)
- for now only non-removable slots (the eMMC) are used
- DMA alignment of one sector: smaller values sent mmc_disk reads through a
  bounce-buffer path that never completed

Pin muxing, clock gates and card power are left as U-Boot set them up.
Built and packaged (with a boot module link) for arm64 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
